-- title:
--   Crossing points of the special fibre: finite and point-determined
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, and assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81), let $\mathrm{Pl}$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $\mathrm{Pl}$, and assume its residue field $\kappa$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed. Let $\rho : R_p \to \mathrm{Pl}$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structural map, giving $\kappa$ the $R_p$-algebra structure via $\rho$ followed by the residue map. Write $Y$ for the fibre over $\kappa$ of the level-$\Gamma_N(p,M,H)$ two-chart integral model, i.e. the pullback of `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` along $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa \to \mathrm{Spec}\,R_p$, with structure morphism $\pi : Y \to \mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$, and let $i_0, i_1$ be the two morphisms `𝔛.comp Pl hPl ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp Pl hPl ρ hρ 1` out of $Y$ attached to $\mathfrak{X}$. Let $P$ be the pullback of $i_0$ along $i_1$, with projections $\mathrm{pr}_1, \mathrm{pr}_2 : P \to Y$, and consider the type of sections, i.e. of morphisms $\varphi : \mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa \to P$ with $\varphi$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_1$ followed by $\pi$ equal to the identity. Granting the hypothesis that $\mathrm{pr}_2$ followed by $\pi$ equals $\mathrm{pr}_1$ followed by $\pi$, the assertion is fourfold: this type of sections is finite; the map sending a section $j$ to the image of the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$ under $j$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_1$ is injective; for every section $j$ one has $i_0 \circ \mathrm{pr}_1 \circ j = i_1 \circ \mathrm{pr}_2 \circ j$; and for all points $q, q'$ of $Y$ with $i_0(q) = i_1(q')$ there is a section $j$ whose closed point maps to $q$ under $\mathrm{pr}_1$ and to $q'$ under $\mathrm{pr}_2$.
--
--   This is the node frame of the geometric special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model at a prime exactly dividing the level: the $\kappa$-points of the crossing scheme of the two components are finite in number, are determined by their image on the first component, and realise exactly those pairs of points on the two components that have the same image. It supplies the finiteness, injectivity and exhaustion inputs used downstream in the analysis of the Néron model of the Jacobian at $p$, namely in [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_schemeHomOver_pts_smul_sub_eq_and_ptsSp_symm_mem_range_nodeUnit_of_mem_inertia_of_abelJacobiPins_of_representsRelSubPic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_schemeHomOver_pts_smul_sub_eq_and_ptsSp_symm_mem_range_nodeUnit_of_mem_inertia_of_abelJacobiPins_of_representsRelSubPic).
